PART 1 — DAILY EXPOSURE CALCULATION IS WRONG FOR ALL CASES (HIGHEST PRIORITY)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

BUG: Across every EI and RS product, per-element/per-solvent Daily Exposure 
values AND their column-sum Totals are wrong. This is the single most 
important production blocker.

Canonical formulas — implement exactly, no shortcuts:

EI Daily Exposure (per element, per component):
   amount_in_max_dose_g = qty_per_unit_mg × doses_per_day × 0.001
   daily_exposure_ug   = amount_in_max_dose_g × concentration_ug_per_g
   (concentration_ug_per_g == ppm, already normalized at extraction)

EI Total (per element, down the column):
   total_daily_exposure_ug = Σ daily_exposure_ug over all non-qs components
   (exclude q.s. rows; include every quantitative component once)

RS Daily Exposure (per solvent, per component):
   amount_in_max_dose_mg = qty_per_unit × multiplier
   daily_exposure_mg     = amount_in_max_dose_mg × solvent_ppm ÷ 1,000,000

RS Total Daily Exposure (per solvent):
   total_mg  = Σ daily_exposure_mg over all contributing components
   equiv_ppm = total_mg × 1,000,000 ÷ drug_product_mass_mg

Root-cause checklist (verify each — the bug is likely one or more of these):
1. Unit mismatch: mg vs g mixup in amount_in_max_dose (×0.001 applied twice, 
   or not at all). Log intermediate amount_in_max_dose for one row and 
   hand-verify.
2. doses_per_day not applied, or applied twice.
3. concentration used in wrong unit (ppb value treated as ppm, or vice versa) 
   — must already be normalized to µg/g before this step.
4. Total row summing the wrong axis (summing across elements instead of down 
   components), or including q.s. rows, or double-counting multi-strength 
   columns.
5. Multi-strength: summing BOTH strength columns instead of the single 
   selected strength (see Part 2/3).

Add a deterministic self-test in code (runs on every generation, logs only):
   Recompute one element's total from raw component values and compare to the 
   emitted total. If |diff| > 0.1%, log ERROR with both values. This catches 
   regressions permanently.

Acceptance (hand-verifiable):
   Take any product, pick one element, manually compute 
   Σ(qty_mg × doses × 0.001 × ppm) across components → must equal the 
   Total cell shown. Every element, every product.

