PART 3 — MDD UNIT + STRENGTH-COLUMN DERIVATION (EI + RS) — user's Q1 & Q2
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Q1 answer (implement): MDD unit and doses/day are DIFFERENT concepts. 
mdd_unit ∈ {mg, units, IU, mcg, mL} describes the drug amount; doses_per_day 
is a COUNT. When mdd_unit == "units" (or continuous infusion), user enters 
MDD in units and leaves doses_per_day = 1. System derives the multiplier / 
daily volume from MDD ÷ API concentration. Never make the user reconcile 
units vs doses.

Q2 answer (implement): The strength column is DERIVED, never forced to max.
   implied_strength = MDD_value ÷ doses_per_day
   Select the composition column whose API strength == implied_strength 
   (nearest match). 
   Example: MDD 120 mg, doses 12 → implied 10 mg → use the 10 mg column 
   (NOT the 40 mg max). Forcing max strength would compute 480 mg/day and 
   contradict the stated MDD of 120 — that is a bug.
   If implied_strength matches NO column within tolerance → warn user 
   ("MDD ÷ doses = X mg does not match any composition strength"), proceed 
   using nearest column, log the choice.
   Regulatory note (do not hardcode, just don't block): the low-strength / 
   high-count scenario can legitimately be the worst case because EI exposure 
   scales with total drug-product MASS/day, not API strength.

REMOVE any "always use maximum strength" logic in both EI and RS. Replace 
with MDD÷doses derivation.

MDD unit → derivation table (EI injection + RS both):
   mdd_unit == "mL":    daily_volume_mL = mdd_value (direct)
   mdd_unit == "mg":    daily_volume_mL = mdd_value ÷ api_conc_mg_per_mL
   mdd_unit == "units": daily_volume_mL = mdd_value ÷ api_units_per_mL
   mdd_unit == "mcg":   convert to mg first, then as mg
   mdd_unit == "IU":    treat as units with product-specific potency
   For solid OSD (mg/tab): multiplier = doses_per_day; strength via MDD÷doses.

Acceptance:
   MDD 120 + doses 12 → 10 mg column selected. 
   Vasopressin MDD 144 units, doses 1 → daily volume = 144 ÷ conc. 
   Chlorpromazine MDD 2400 mg → daily volume = 2400 ÷ 25 = 96 mL.

