PART 5 — ANNEXURE NAME FALLBACK: NEVER "residual solvent" / GENERIC (ALL 4 TYPES)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

BUG: RS annexure converter emits generic titles like "residual solvent" 
(the document TYPE, not the material) into the annexure list when it can't 
find a real material name. Applies across doc types — must be fixed everywhere.

Fix — annexure DISPLAY name resolution (payload/renderer layer), priority:
1. The COMPOSITION ingredient name it matched to (EI/RS/DEG-EG — clean, 
   scientist-typed).
2. Cleaned annexure material_name (strip vendor grade/purity/compendia noise).
3. Filename-derived name: strip "Annexure N", extension, SAP codes, dates, 
   and DOCUMENT-TYPE words ("residual solvent", "elemental impurity", 
   "DEG", "EG", "risk assessment", "declaration", "certificate of analysis", 
   "specification", "statement", "CoA").
4. "Material [N]".

NEVER emit a document-type/descriptor word as a material name. Add a reject 
list of descriptor tokens; if the resolved name IS only a descriptor, fall 
through to the next priority.

Backend MATCHING still uses all messy text (title, candidates, filename) — 
no change to matching. Only DISPLAY is cleaned.

BE NOC: uses annexure-type classification titles (no composition Excel) — 
keep existing, but still apply the "never show a bare descriptor" rule and 
filename fallback.

Acceptance:
   RS Chlorpromazine annexures show ingredient names (or vendor material), 
   never "residual solvent". DEG/EG never shows "DEG/EG declaration" as a 
   material. EI never shows "elemental impurity". Filename fallback strips 
   descriptor words.

