PART 7 — PAGE NUMBERS EMPTY (all doc types where annexure page refs used)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

BUG: page-number list comes back empty. Exact per-solvent/element source page 
is hard, but empty list is unacceptable for production.

Fix:
1. Record the source page index during multi-page extraction (the page a 
   value/table was found on). Attach page number to each extracted 
   element/solvent record at extraction time.
2. Roll up to per-annexure page ranges: {"annexure_pages": "1-3"} minimum.
3. If per-field page cannot be determined, fall back to the annexure's total 
   page span (e.g., "pp. 1–6") rather than an empty list.
4. Never emit an empty page list — always at least the annexure page span.

Acceptance: every annexure carries a non-empty page reference (specific page 
if known, else full span).

