PART 8 — FONT SIZE INVERSION (all renderers)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

BUG: Section HEADINGS render SMALL and body CONTENT renders LARGE — inverted, 
looks broken.

Fix in generate_*.js (all 4 renderers):
- Headings > body. Enforce a size hierarchy:
   Doc title:      ~26–28 half-points equivalent (largest)
   Section heading:~22–24, bold
   Sub-heading:    ~20, bold
   Body text:      ~20–22 (SMALLER than or equal to headings, never larger)
   Table cell:     ~18–20
- Audit every run.* / heading builder for swapped size constants. The bug is 
  almost certainly a size constant applied to the wrong element (heading using 
  the body size and vice versa).

Acceptance: in all 4 doc types, headings are visibly larger/bolder than body; 
no funny inversion.

