PART 9 — SALT/BASE & OVERAGE FOOTNOTE (EI + RS) — reconfirm for these products
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Carboprost "# 332 mcg tromethamine ≡ 250 mcg carboprost" → salt/base:
   base_qty=250mcg, salt_qty=332mcg, salt_factor=1.328.
   Multiplier uses BASE; component amount uses SALT weight.
Chlorpromazine HCl: MDD and strength both salt-basis → NO salt conversion; 
   "#" on vendor is informational (Category D). Warning-only footnote check 
   passes. Do not ask for salt_factor.
Rule (already built, verify wired for EI too, not just RS): parse Excel marker 
footnotes, classify salt/base vs overage vs q.s. vs informational, auto-set 
salt_factor/overage; warning-only if missing; default 1.0. Applies to EI AND 
RS.

